  "response": "{\n  \"primary_cause\": \"insufficient_model_capacity\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"candidate_ranking\": [\n    \"insufficient_model_capacity\",\n    \"insufficient_state_action_coverage\",\n    \"action_conditioning_failure\",\n    \"dynamics_distribution_shift\",\n    \"optimization_instability\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_for\": [\n    \"The initial configuration featured an extreme architectural bottleneck (model.hidden_width: 2, model.hidden_values: [32, 32]), which fundamentally restricted representation power for continuous Reacher kinematics.\",\n    \"Executing EXP_CAP to increase hidden width to [64, 64] while holding data collection constant yielded substantial improvements: train_final_loss decreased from 0.540 to 0.383, step_5_mse dropped from 10.234 to 3.250, and one_step_mse improved from 4.692 to 3.939.\",\n    \"The direct correlation between increased model capacity and reduced prediction error across both short and medium horizons confirms that architectural constraints were the primary driver of the observed generalization gap.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_against\": [\n    \"Optimization stability metrics remain consistent throughout (lr_vs_typical_ratio: 1.0, smooth train loss convergence), effectively ruling out optimization_instability as a contributing factor.\",\n    \"While data.n_episodes: 8 and data.action_mode: biased suggest potential coverage limitations, the significant performance gains achieved solely by widening the network indicate that data scarcity is secondary to the initial structural bottleneck.\"\n  ],\n  \"missing_evidence\": [\n    \"Performance benchmarks on uniformly sampled datasets to isolate and quantify the independent impact of action_mode bias.\",\n    \"Ablation studies mapping error scaling across intermediate hidden widths (e.g., [32,32], [48,48]) to establish precise capacity thresholds for this task.\",\n    \"Evaluation under expanded target distributions to determine if remaining generalization gaps at longer horizons (step_10_mse: 9.237) stem from residual coverage issues or deeper architectural limits.\"\n  ],\n  \"information_gain\": \"The discriminative experiment successfully isolated model capacity as the dominant failure mode. By holding data collection constant and only increasing hidden width, we observed a marked reduction in both single-step and multi-step prediction errors, confirming that the initial narrow architecture was the primary constraint preventing accurate dynamics learning.\",\n  \"abstain\": false\n}",
